{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Tests written and pushed as Gerrit change 1725 (sha 33d2566334), tests-only: +181 lines across tests/scripts/graph/test_graph_cycles.py and tests/scripts/test_ticket_unblock.py, no src/rebar change.\n\nCharacterization verified by mutation, each new test goes red for exactly its branch and green again on revert:\n- delete the _is_at_level call in _same_level_neighbors -> test_check_cycle_at_level_refuses_a_target_at_another_level fails (verdict flips False -> True).\n- delete the state-is-None + tombstone stub branch -> test_unreducible_dir_with_a_tombstone_yields_a_status_only_stub fails ([] -> ['tkt-target']).\n- delete the state['status'] = tombstone_status override -> test_tombstone_status_overrides_the_reduced_status fails (['tkt-target'] -> []).\n- make _read_tombstone_status's except return None -> test_malformed_tombstone_degrades_to_deleted_not_to_absent fails (['tkt-target'] -> []).\n\nTwo findings worth recording, neither a defect:\n1. The two level guards in _same_level_neighbors are NOT interchangeable. An epic -> task -> epic hop is already refused by the inline current-side ticket_type check, so it stays False even with _is_at_level deleted. Only a DIRECT cross-level edge whose far end is source_id is sensitive to the target-side guard. The hop test is kept as an end-to-end pin but it is the direct test that covers the guard.\n2. The reduce-returns-None + tombstone stub is observable through detect_newly_unblocked ONLY when the recorded status is non-terminal. With a terminal status the stub and 'no entry at all' are indistinguishable, because _is_closed_after_batch treats a missing dir as closed. The test therefore uses a tombstone recording 'open' and pins that _read_tombstone_status propagates .get('status', 'deleted') verbatim with no validation. Real tombstones written by rebar delete always record 'deleted'.\n\nNo defect found, so no discovered_from bug filed. Local gates green: all check_* scripts, complexity baseline, make lint, make typecheck, make config-check, the four doc generators produce no diff, and the CI suite (not integration and not external, -n 3) is 12730 passed / 60 skipped. Two errors in that run were the HEAD-movement guard firing because the commit landed mid-run; re-running those two files against a stable HEAD gives 49 passed."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786618927776494001,"uuid":"fdecc41b-5c84-45cc-88dc-c2ccea914dca"}